        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Angkor</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">889 CE – c. 1431 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Angkorian period began around 800 CE with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jayavarman-ii">Jayavarman II</a>; the city of Yasodharapura, centred on Phnom Bakheng, was built by Yasovarman, who ascended the throne in 889.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">Amid forests and farmland north of the Great Lake (Tonlé Sap) and south of the Kulen Hills, near the present city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siem-reap">Siem Reap</a> in Siem Reap Province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a>.</span></div>
